# This ChangeLog is a fork of Alibaba Cloud NimoShake's.
# Entries tagged "-sc*" are StarCo builds, not upstream releases.
# Upstream history below 2025-07-04 is preserved verbatim.

2026-09-17
	* VERSION: 1.0.14-sc.20260917-OPAPP
	* BASE: 1.0.14-sc.20260818 (StarCo mchange_cast + nimo-full-check rewrite)
	* CONTRACT: contract-2026-09-11.1 (embedded in both binaries' version
	  strings; nimo-shake -version / nimo-full-check --version also carry
	  nssrc= / fcsrc= source fingerprints)
	* FEATURE: type rules schema v2 (collection-scoped) — rules are keyed by
	  table + top-level field; same field name in different tables is
	  governed independently. type_rules_opapp.json declares 23 collections
	  (20 governed + 3 preserve-only) and 43 rules (33 int32, 10 int64).
	  v1 rule files are rejected by this build (startup summary prints
	  schema=v1 ... scope_database=unbound); v2 files are rejected by the
	  previous build — the two formats are mutually exclusive
	* FEATURE: int32/int64 cast parses the raw DynamoDB N literal exactly
	  (no float64 round-trip); values above 2^53 and the full int64 range
	  are written exactly. Non-integer / out-of-range / non-N sources keep
	  the original value and are reported as SOURCE_UNCASTABLE
	* FEATURE: numeric-string seqno (allow_numeric_string) enabled on 5
	  rules only (egtc_traded_m, event_record_traded_m,
	  external_import_traded_m, imm_traded_m, mms_coupon_m). Only canonical
	  decimal integer literals are cast; leading zero ("007"), negative zero
	  ("-0"), signs, whitespace, fractions and non-digits are rejected and
	  the original string is preserved. Exceptions carry a reason field
	  (LEADING_ZERO / NEGATIVE_ZERO / INVALID_INTEGER / FRACTIONAL /
	  OUT_OF_RANGE / TYPE_MISMATCH). No switch relaxes this
	* FEATURE: nimo-shake startup preflight — rejects start (before any
	  checkpoint or target mutation) when rules scope.database != conf id,
	  when the resolved table list != the 23 declared collections
	  (missing / extra / typo are all rejected with missing=[] extra=[]
	  detail), or when a governed field collides with a table's partition /
	  sort key. Empty white AND black list = sync everything; the resolved
	  list is still validated against the contract
	* FEATURE: startup summary (3 lines, printed once per process) with
	  schema, config_id, config_version, database, collection counts, rule
	  count and rules_sha256; nimo-full-check prints the same summary
	* FEATURE: checkpoint rule fingerprint — status document additionally
	  records rules_sha256, config_version, convert.type, convert._id and
	  database; resuming from incr_sync with any field different exits with
	  an error (no resume, no full re-sync, no drop). Only the incr_sync
	  resume path is protected: re-running full with a changed rule file is
	  not blocked and rebuilds collections per target.db.exist
	* FEATURE: nimo-full-check rule-coverage completeness gate —
	  rule-coverage.json now registers exactly the 43 per-table rules (was
	  989 cross-product rows); any governed rule with zero_hits sets
	  coverage_complete=false and promotes the run to EXECUTION_ERROR
	  (exit 2). A rule with no convertible observation keeps a FAIL /
	  PASS_WITH_EXCEPTIONS result but promotes a bare PASS to exit 2.
	  Any --resume run is marked resume_partial_observations and never
	  counts as a completeness proof (a resumed PASS becomes exit 2)
	* BUGFIX: type-conversion module log output is now routed to the
	  configured log file (previous build's converter INFO/WARN never
	  reached nimo-shake.log)
	* NOTE: binaries are dynamically linked (go1.20.14, CGO enabled); the
	  target host needs a compatible glibc. The previous package described
	  nimo-full-check as static — that no longer applies
	* NOTE: incremental sync (sync_mode=all), shard handoff, CheckCkpt
	  resume decisions and the fingerprint-mismatch rejection were NOT
	  exercised in the lab (DynamoDB Local requires source.endpoint_url,
	  which restricts the product to sync_mode=full). See
	  docs/驗證報告_2026-09-17.md for the customer-environment checklist
	* NOTE: nimo-shake.linux    -version  -> OPAPP-nimoshake,contract=contract-2026-09-11.1,nssrc=2c8869a686165d3d06cbf87d710b8300273bd371e45aec4730ab1082a2f1a8fb,fcsrc=3cd42bf1f0254ba4bf30f4c8ce264939ef19bca455fe282ab0f4a75b6c62ee16,2026-09-17T02:40:24Z
	*       nimo-full-check.linux --version -> OPAPP-fullcheck,contract=contract-2026-09-11.1,src=unknown,fcsrc=3cd42bf1f0254ba4bf30f4c8ce264939ef19bca455fe282ab0f4a75b6c62ee16,nssrc=2c8869a68616,2026-09-17_10:39:10
	*       (file hashes: see SHA256SUMS)

2026-08-18
	* VERSION: 1.0.14-sc.20260818
	* BASE: upstream nimo-shake 1.0.14 (2025-07-04)
	* FEATURE: add convert.type=mchange_cast — rule-driven type casting before
	  write (float64->int32/bool, string->ISODate) via convert.type_rules_path
	  (type_rules_nimoshake.json, 27 managed fields); removes the need for
	  Atlas Database Trigger post-processing
	* BUGFIX: fix Array-parent element casting under mchange_cast
	  (c_order_d / e_shipment_l / e_shipment_s)
	* FEATURE: nimo-full-check fully rewritten — per-field BSON type
	  verification, bidirectional check (-m both), checkpoint/--resume,
	  segment sampling, batch query + QPS limiting, rule-coverage.json,
	  run-manifest.json, converge recheck for replication lag
	  (TRANSIENT_CONVERGED; safe to run during incremental sync)
	* BUGFIX: nimo-full-check no longer produces false "0 diff" reports
	  (2025-07-04 binary had --sample=0=disabled semantics and type-blind
	  comparison; do NOT use the old binary)
	* REFINE: start.sh — correct binary name (was ./dynamo-shake), drop
	  obsolete -type argument (accepted but ignored with a warning), default
	  conf, preflight checks (binary/conf/type_rules/duplicate start), report
	  startup failure with log tail instead of failing silently
	* REFINE: stop.sh — verify pid identity before kill (PID-reuse guard),
	  TERM before KILL, "already finished" treated as success
	* REMOVE: hypervisor — shipped binary was Mach-O (never ran on Linux);
	  its unconditional-restart loop is unsafe with sync_mode=full +
	  target.db.exist=drop (would repeatedly wipe and re-sync the target).
	  Replaced by setsid nohup daemonization in start.sh
	* REMOVE: darwin binaries (target environment is Linux; no macOS
	  verification environment available)
	* NOTE: nimo-shake.linux    -version  -> (2026-07-09 build, no embedded version string; identify via SHA256SUMS)
	*       nimo-full-check.linux --version -> mbec-fullcheck,src=1a676b7,2026-08-17_10:40:40

2025-07-04
	* VERSION: 1.0.14
    * IMPROVE: adapt shard split scene
    * REFINE: upgrade to go1.15.10 with mod to compile
    * REFINE: close writer when all writes are done
    * REFINE: delete useless bin files in project
    * IMPROVE: update shard status to finish when all incr data have written to dest DB
    * IMPROVE: wait for father shard in executor because of we are caching incremental data
    * REFINE: modify Node channel size, no need for large chan anymore when don't use memory cache
    * IMPROVE: incr cache file persist to db
    * IMPROVE: add parameter 'increase.persist.dir'
    * REFINE: deprecate mgo, replace it with mongo-driver
    * IMPROVE: add api qos
    * BUGFIX: fix index ele type parse
    * IMPROVE: support MongoDB 6.0+
    * IMPROVE: support DynamoDB filter_expression

